  "difficulty_reason": "H2: the author alternates two nonroutine regularity gains. A vertical variation gives the two-phase transmission condition; flattening the interface and differentiating tangentially brings in transmission estimates to raise solution regularity. A separate shape variation derives a weighted mean-curvature equation whose denominator needs the proven positive lower bound, raising interface regularity by one derivative. The complete coupled bootstrap and the old positivity/Hölder core are supplied, rather than assuming a smooth interface.",
